# Passenger rights when a flight is disrupted.
# A domain deliberately far from a D&D fight: entitlements, exceptions and
# duties rather than actors, turns and damage.
#
# A disruption is NEWS -- it happens to a schedule that was otherwise going
# to run -- so it arrives on a channel rather than sitting as a loaded
# `fact`: attention is *taking care of something*, and a loaded fact is
# background nobody has been asked to take care of (§20). `<trust>` is the
# whole of the crossing, generic over the relation (`$p` binds the WHOLE
# said thing, `guide.md`'s `$p($x)` idiom one level up) because this
# corpus has exactly one channel and nothing adversarial to filter.
rule <trust>
  +says($ch, $p)
  no trusted($ch, $p)
->
  +trusted($ch, $p)
  +$p

# `<intake>` (the bundle's own crossing) writes `says(...)` as an ordinary
# move's ordinary conclusion, so it fades at a brush's one tick like
# anything else a rule happens to write. Two flights land in the same
# batch of arrivals, so `<trust>` has more than one saying to catch, and a
# brush's one tick is not enough runway for the second to survive being
# the sibling that lost this round. `after` re-attends the REAL believed
# node (a match, never a rebuild -- `$sp` binds what `<intake>` this
# application actually wrote) at the same strength the arrival itself
# carries in (§20). The same hop happens again one rule later --
# `<trust>`'s own `+$p` is again an ordinary write -- so `<cancel>`,
# `<weather>` and the rest each get the same runway to find their premise,
# rather than `<weather>` losing its one tick to whichever of `<cancel>`/
# `<late>`/`<compensate>` the table happens to score higher that round.
# `<compensate>` reading `no extraordinary($f)` before `<weather>` ever
# ran is exactly the corpus's own "raj is compensated for a storm" failure
# mode, and it is an ATTENTION race, not a declared-order one: a rule
# scored higher by `_pull` is tried FIRST regardless of authored order,
# and authored order only breaks a TIE.
after <intake> { $sp = says($channel, $said) } => attend($sp, 5, 1, 1)
after <trust> { $tp = $p } => attend($tp, 5, 1, 1)

rule <cancel>
  +cancelled($f)
  no disrupted($f)
->
  +disrupted($f)
rule <late>
  +delayed($f, long)
  no disrupted($f)
->
  +disrupted($f)
# ...and one hop further still: `<care>`/`<compensate>`/`<reroute>` all
# read `disrupted($f)`, and with TWO flights disrupted there are two of
# them to catch. Same fix, same reason -- see the header comment above.
after <cancel> { $dp = disrupted($f) } => attend($dp, 5, 1, 1)
after <late> { $dp = disrupted($f) } => attend($dp, 5, 1, 1)

# the duty of care is owed whatever the cause
#
# A move consumes its premises, and `<compensate>` and `<reroute>` below
# need the same two -- so without putting them back, the first rule to
# reach a disruption is the only one that ever does, and compensation is
# never asked about at all.
#
# `brush(disrupted($f))` on the tail was tried here and does NOT do that:
# `$f` is an ARGUMENT this rule bound, and the tail rebuilds `disrupted($f)`
# from it by substitution -- which MINTS a twin (`rel` does not intern),
# never the node this rule actually matched. `after` reaches the real one
# because its query is a MATCH, not a rebuild -- the same reason the
# `<intake>`/`<trust>` hops above use it rather than a tail `brush(...)`.
rule <care>
  +disrupted($f)
  +booked($p, $f)
  no owed($p, meals)
->
  +owed($p, meals)
  +owed($p, lodging)
after <care> { $dp = disrupted($f), $bp = booked($p, $f) }
  => attend($dp, 5, 1, 1), attend($bp, 5, 1, 1)

# a storm is outside the carrier's control; a crew shortage is not, and that is
# now said by the ABSENCE of a rule rather than by one.
rule <weather>
  +cause($f, storm)
  no extraordinary($f)
->
  +extraordinary($f)

# ...but compensation is not, if the cause was outside the carrier's control.
# This is `unless`, written where a rule's variables live.
#
# `no extraordinary($f)` and not `-extraordinary($f)`. The two used to be one
# mark, and a `-` premise meant *something denies this* rather than *nothing
# says it*. There is nothing left to deny with, so a corpus has to choose, and
# here the honest reading is absence: a flight is ordinary until something says
# otherwise. That also deletes a rule -- `<crewing>` concluded
# `-extraordinary($f)` to say a crew shortage is the carrier's own problem, and
# under absence there is nothing to conclude, because not saying it IS saying it.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING HERE, and it was not before. `no` is asked of the state
# as it stands at the moment of the match, and nothing now guarantees that
# everything which could make `extraordinary($f)` true has been settled first.
# The old engine had a stratification pass that computed exactly that order and
# refused a corpus whose negations had no such order; it belonged to the second
# matcher, and it went when the second matcher did. So `<weather>` is authored
# ABOVE this rule deliberately: authored order is the arbitration tiebreak, so
# a storm is recognised before compensation is asked about. Written the other
# way round, raj is compensated for a storm -- measured, not supposed.
rule <compensate>
  +disrupted($f)
  +booked($p, $f)
  no extraordinary($f)
  no owed($p, money)
->
  +owed($p, money)
# `<reroute>` further down still needs both, so the relay continues.
after <compensate> { $dp = disrupted($f), $bp = booked($p, $f) }
  => attend($dp, 5, 1, 1), attend($bp, 5, 1, 1)

# the amount depends on how far the passenger was going
rule <far>
  +owed($p, money)
  +flying($p, $f)
  +distance($f, long)
  no amount($p, 600)
->
  +amount($p, 600)
rule <near>
  +owed($p, money)
  +flying($p, $f)
  +distance($f, short)
  no amount($p, 250)
->
  +amount($p, 250)

# re-routing: a seat on another service to the same place
rule <reroute>
  +disrupted($f)
  +booked($p, $f)
  +goes($f, $dest)
  +goes($g, $dest)
  +seats_free($g)
  no rerouted($p, $g)
->
  +rerouted($p, $g)

say ops: +cancelled(bl204)
say ops: +cause(bl204, crew)
fact +booked(ana, bl204)
fact +flying(ana, bl204)
fact +distance(bl204, long)
fact +goes(bl204, lisbon)

say ops: +delayed(kt881, long)
say ops: +cause(kt881, storm)
fact +booked(raj, kt881)
fact +flying(raj, kt881)
fact +distance(kt881, short)

fact +goes(zr9, lisbon)
fact +seats_free(zr9)
